    },
    {
      "title": "Zelenskyy furious as Trump announces deal to buy Russian diesel",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/09/trump-putin-russian-diesel-ukraine",
      "description": "<p>President says deal essential to lower US fuel prices but move set to create fresh crisis with Ukraine and Nato allies</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/oct/09/pentagon-fort-hood-livestream-firing-squad-execution-reaction-backlash-pete-hegseth-donald-trump-mussolini-latest-news-updates\">US politics – live updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Donald Trump was on a fresh collision course with the Ukrainian president, Volodymyr Zelenskyy, and European allies on Friday after a stunning agreement to buy Russian diesel, upending years of US and western pressure on the Kremlin to end its four-and-a-half year war against Ukraine.</p><p>Zelenskyy reacted furiously to Trump’s announcement of the deal with President Vladimir Putin of Russia, <a href=\"https://www.axios.com/2026/10/09/exclusive-zelensky-putin-trump-diesel-deal?stream=top&amp;utm_source=alert&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=alerts_all&amp;lctg=5887fe39cb4a2b33558b4f0b\">calling it</a> “absolutely terrible” and “not fair and not honest”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/09/trump-putin-russian-diesel-ukraine\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-09T23:39:31"
    },
    {
      "title": "Pete Hegseth’s plan to livestream execution puts US in dubious company",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/09/pete-hegseth-public-execution-nidal-hasan-capital-sentences",
      "description": "<p>Only Iran and Afghanistan routinely carry out sentences in public, with Saudi Arabia appearing to have ended practice</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/oct/09/pentagon-fort-hood-livestream-firing-squad-execution-reaction-backlash-pete-hegseth-donald-trump-mussolini-latest-news-updates\">US politics – live updates</a></p></li></ul><p>If the US defence secretary, Pete Hegseth, goes ahead with plans to <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/08/hegseth-fort-hood-shooter-public-execution\">livestream the execution</a> of a soldier radicalised to extremist Islam who killed 13 people at a military base in Texas, his country will join a motley assembly of lesser powers and rogue actors who have conducted public executions in recent years.</p><p>Only two countries currently systematically carry out capital sentences in public: Iran and Afghanistan. In 2025, the Taliban authorities carried out six such killings and the regime in Tehran 11, according to Amnesty International.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/09/pete-hegseth-public-execution-nidal-hasan-capital-sentences\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-09T13:55:07"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘I want to thank President Putin’, Trump says after agreeing to lift sanctions on Russian diesel – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/oct/09/pentagon-fort-hood-livestream-firing-squad-execution-reaction-backlash-pete-hegseth-donald-trump-mussolini-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>This liveblog is now closed.</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/09/trump-putin-russian-diesel-ukraine\">Zelenskyy furious as Trump announces deal to buy Russian diesel</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/news/2026/feb/17/sign-up-for-the-breaking-news-us-email-to-get-newsletter-alerts-direct-to-your-inbox?utm_medium=ACQUISITIONS_STANDFIRST&amp;utm_campaign=BN22326&amp;utm_content=signup&amp;utm_term=standfirst&amp;utm_source=GUARDIAN_WEB\">Sign up for the US Breaking News email</a></p></li></ul><p>In a statement to the Guardian, <strong>Robin M</strong><strong> Maher</strong>, the executive director of the Death Penalty Information Center, said that her group is <strong>“not aware of any regulation or precedent for a military execution to be live</strong><strong>streamed</strong> on the internet or otherwise made widely available to the public”.</p><p>She added that <strong>“public executions are typically held in authoritarian countries to instil fear in the population, and to show the power and control of the government.”</strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/oct/09/pentagon-fort-hood-livestream-firing-squad-execution-reaction-backlash-pete-hegseth-donald-trump-mussolini-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-10T02:02:45"
    },
