    {
      "title": "US lifts Russian diesel sanctions until Apr 7, 2027, after Trump-Putin call",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/us-lifts-russian-diesel-sanctions-until-apr-7-2027-after-trump-putin-call-126101000046_1.html",
      "description": "The US on Friday lifted sanctions on the sale of Russian diesel till April 7 next year.\nThe announcement by the US Department of Treasury came minutes after US President Donald Trump spoke with Russian President Vladimir Putin and struck a deal to supply diesel to the American and global markets.\n\"...all transactions prohibited by the Russian Harmful Foreign Activities Sanctions Regulations  that are related to the sale, delivery, offloading, or importation, including importation into the United States, of diesel fuel of Russian Federation origin are authorised through 12:01 am eastern daylight time, April 7, 2027,\" the Treasury Department said.\nEarlier, Trump said Russia will immediately supply more than 300,000 tons of diesel, followed by 500,000 tons in November, and one million tons immediately thereafter.\nRussia will then deliver another 3 million tons of diesel based on the condition of Russia's refineries, Trump said in a post on Truth Social.\nDiesel prices have surged arou",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-10T02:32:33"
    },
    {
      "title": "Trump strikes deal with Putin to supply Russian diesel to U.S. and global markets",
